    "probe_text": "Here is everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. The behavior is spread across MVC advice, Bean Validation, MapStruct mappers, AspectJ aspects around the service, and JPA \u2014 there is *no* single method that contains it all.\n\n## Phase A \u2014 RequestBody advice (after Jackson deserialization, before `@Valid`)\n\nAll of these run on the deserialized `OwnerFieldsDto`. Every one is `@Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)`, so **their order relative to each other is not deterministic from the code** \u2014 this matters where mutation and validation touch the same field.\n\n**Mutations (side-effects on the DTO):**\n1. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 rewrite to E.164: strip non-digits; if no `+`, drop leading `0` and prepend `61` (AU). Must be 8\u201315 digits (else 400 `InvalidTelephone`); `+61` must have 9 national digits, `+1` must have 10 (else 400).\n2. **Email normalization** \u2014 `strip().toLowerCase()`, must match email regex (else 400 `InvalidEmail`).\n3. **Address normalization** \u2014 trim/collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n4. **Registration date defaulting** \u2014 `registrationDate` defaults to today if absent; Sat/Sun roll forward to Monday.\n\n**Validations (reject before persistence):**\n5. **Required fields** \u2014 firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone non-blank (else 400 `MissingOwnerFields`).\n6. **Disposable email** \u2014 reject mailinator.com / tempmail.com / guerrillamail.com (400).\n7. **Postcode/city consistency** \u2014 for Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane, postcode must fall in the region band (2000/3000/4000 +99) (400).\n8. **Future registration date** \u2014 supplied date after today (400).\n9. **Household duplicate** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold==true`, compute `householdId` = SHA-256(lastName+postcode)[:12] and scan `findAllOwners()`; match \u2192 **409** `DuplicateHousehold`.\n10. **Unique identity** \u2014 `normalizedTelephone|email` compared against all owners; exact match \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentity`.\n11. **Daily creation limit** \u2014 \u2265100 owners with same effective business-day date \u2192 **429** `DailyLimitReached`.\n12. **City capacity** \u2014 \u226550 owners in same normalized city \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacity`.\n\n## Phase B \u2014 Bean Validation (`@Valid`)\n13. Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`: `firstName`/`lastName` (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size` 1\u201330), `address` (1\u2013255), `city` (1\u201380), `telephone` (`@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, 1\u201320), `email` (`@Size` \u2264255, nullable), `postcode` (`@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`, nullable). Failures \u2192 400.\n\n## Phase C \u2014 Mapping\n14. `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` builds a new `Owner` (id/pets left null \u2192 `isNew()==true`).\n\n## Phase D \u2014 Aspects around `clinicService.saveOwner` (order among these also non-deterministic \u2014 no `@Order`)\n15. **Household size** \u2014 if new & null, count owners sharing householdId, set `householdSize = existing+1`.\n16. **Namesake count** \u2014 if new & null, count owners with same first+last (case-insensitive), set `namesakeCount`.\n17. **Customer code** \u2014 if new & null, set `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode band; hash = SHA-256(telephone+lastName)[:4 bytes]).\n18. **Audit** (`@Around`) \u2014 after the save, if it was new, log `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026` to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n## Phase E \u2014 Persistence\n19. `saveOwner` is `@Transactional`; `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.save` \u2192 `em.persist` (id is null). Hibernate re-validates entity `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` at flush; transaction commits.\n\n## Phase F \u2014 Response side (not persisted, but applied on the way out)\n20. `toOwnerDto` derives display-only fields: displayName, initials, householdId, identityKey, checkDigit, membershipNumber/points/level, locality, contactPreference, ageBand, telephoneDisplay.\n21. **ResponseBodyAdvice**: `bulkSignupWarning = (owners registered today > 80)`; force `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`.\n22. Return **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Cross-cutting\n- **Security**: `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`. No password encoding occurs (owners have no password).\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks / Spring Data auditing** exist \u2014 all defaulting/audit is done by the aspects above, not `@PrePersist`/`@CreatedDate`.\n- **Ordering caveat**: because all RequestBody advices share `HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE` and the save-time aspects have no `@Order`, the exact sequence within Phase A and within Phase D is unspecified by the code."
